# s4-engine-actions-observe-nav desktop wiring (host side of the engine lane)

The Rust actions of native/core/crates/mixdog-browser-engine/src/actions/{observe,navigation,flow,diagnostics}.rs ask the host for three things the host does not serve yet.
The host files belong to the host tasks, not to this one.

## 1. `host/browser/cdp/send` allowlist (apps/desktop/src/main/host/browser-engine/cdp-send.ts, CDP_SEND_ALLOWED)
Add, read-side only:
- `Page.printToPDF` with params {printBackground: true}: the old `snapshot mode=visual format=pdf` printed through `guest.printToPDF({ printBackground: true })` because the
  embedded debugger does not carry the CDP method. The host must serve the method through its own printer and answer `{ result: { data: <base64> } }`, or, when the
  PDF is larger than the inline limit, `{ result: { blob: { digest, size } } }` (registry.ts `fitResult` only moves a top-level `data`; a `cdp/send` result nests it
  under `result`, so the handler itself must upload the bytes with uploadBlob). The engine reads either form and refuses a PDF over 100 MiB.
- `Network.getRequestPostData` and `Network.getResponseBody` with {requestId} and the request's `sessionId` (the child target of the request, absent for the page's own):
  the `network` action with a `requestId` shows a request's bodies, as network-report.ts did through `cdp.call`. A refused or failed call is shown as "Response body is no longer
  available from Chromium." The bodies are masked by the registry like every string of a result.

## 2. `host/browser/page/read` (apps/desktop/src/main/host/browser-engine/page.ts, `read`)
The engine applies `query`, `offset` and `maxChars` of the `read` action itself to the page text the host answers (up to READ_MAX_CHARS_WIRE = 120,000 characters, `truncated`
says when the page has more), and says so in the reply when the text was cut at that limit. A page with more text than that cannot be read past 120,000 characters; to lift it,
`BrowserPageReadOptions` needs `offset` (and the host `readPage(guest, query, maxChars, offset)` it already has). For `extract` the host answers the six attributes of
READ_SELECTOR_ATTRIBUTES; the engine shows those among the ones the command named, so an attribute outside that list is not shown until `BrowserPageReadOptions` carries
`attributes` and `limit`. Neither field exists in the protocol today; this is a follow-up for the protocol and host tasks, not a change this task needed to compile.

## 3. Nothing else
`navigate`/`back` use `host/browser/page/navigate` as served (url, reload, back with `refused`), `locate` uses `page/eval`, `snapshot` modes use `screenshot` (with a ref clip for an element).
